It might be impossible, but a nicer way of doing this would be to modify VitePress's router, but I couldn't figure out if there was an easy way of doing this:

```js
import DefaultTheme from 'vitepress/theme'

export default {
  ...DefaultTheme,
  enhanceApp(ctx) {
    DefaultTheme.enhanceApp(ctx)
    
    // can we do something with this?
    // I can't find anything in the API, see https://github.com/vuejs/vitepress/blob/main/src/client/app/router.ts
    const {router} = ctx;
  }
}
```

It could be worth making a feature request issue on VitePress for this.
